ler crews. The Yngling was designed in 1967 by Norwegian designer Jan Linde, who also designed the Soling. The Yngling was raced at the 2000-08 Olympics, but was replaced in 2012 by the Elliott 6 metre class for women."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The British boat skippered by " [:a {:href "/athletes/61039"} "Shirley Robertson"] " won only two races but still built up such a big lead that it was able to skip the final race and win the gold medal. This was Robertson’s second Olympic gold medal, having won the 2000 Europe Class at Sydney. Runner-up helmsperson " [:a {:href "/athletes/61065"} "Ruslana Taran"] " of Ukraine won her third consecutive Olympic medal, after bronzes in the 470 at the 1996 and 2000 Olympics."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Net Points"] [:th {} "Total Points"] [:th {} "Race #1"] [:th {} "Race #2"] [:th {} "Race #3"] [:th {} "Race #4"] [:th {} "Race #5"] [:th {} "Race #6"] [:th {} "Race #7"] [:th {} "Race #8"] [:th {} "Race #9"] [:th {} "Race #10"] [:th {} "Race #11"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "Great Britain"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {} "39.0"] [:td {} "56.0"] [:td {} "5.0 (5)"] [:td {} "4.0 (4)"] [:td {} "1.0 (1)"] [:td {} "1.0 (1)"] [:td {} "4.0 (4)"] [:td {} "3.0 (3)"] [:td {} "4.0 (4)"] [:td {} "6.0 (6)"] [:td {} "3.0 (3)"] [:td {} "8.0 (8)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "21"} [:a {:href "/athletes/61039"} "Shirley Robertson"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/103972"} "Sarah Webb"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/103973"} "Sarah Ayton"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} "Ukraine"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/UKR"} [:img {:style "padding-ri